## 2. MEMORY LEAKS

### 2a. SearchButton.svelte -- MutationObserver and addEventListener never cleaned up
**File**: `src\lib\ui\navigators\buttons\SearchButton.svelte`, lines 38-44

```svelte
const observer = new MutationObserver(checkForNavigation);
observer.observe(document.body, {
  childList: true,
  subtree: true
});

window.addEventListener("popstate", updateSearchState);
```

This code runs at module scope (not inside `onMount`). There is no `onDestroy` or any cleanup. The MutationObserver watches `document.body` with `subtree: true` -- this is both a memory leak and a performance problem (firing on every DOM mutation in the entire page). The `popstate` listener also leaks.

