```

This listener is never removed. While the anonymous arrow function makes removal impossible anyway, the listener persists after component unmount.

### 2d. Video.svelte -- setTimeout without cleanup
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\Video.svelte`, lines 16-19

```svelte
onMount(() =&gt; {
  setTimeout(() =&gt; {
    showVime = true;
  }, 500);
});
```

The timeout is not cleared on destroy. If the component unmounts within 500ms, it will still try to set state on a destroyed component.

### 2e. Presence service WebSocket connections never closed
**File**: `src\lib\services\community\services\presence.svelte.ts`

`startPresenceListener` creates a new `PartySocket` on line 60 each time it is called but never closes the previous connection. If called multiple times (e.g., navigating between courses on the live page), old WebSocket connections remain open. There is no `close()` call anywhere in the service.

### 2f. Connect service timer started but never stopped on navigation
**File**: `src\routes\(course-reader)\+layout.svelte`, line 12

```svelte
tutorsConnectService.startTimer();
```

This starts a 30-second `setInterval` but there is no corresponding `onDestroy` that calls `stopTimer()`. While the timer does have a `stopTimer()` method, it is never called from any component.

