### 4a. Svelte 4 vs Svelte 5 event handler syntax mixed
**File**: `src\lib\ui\navigators\buttons\SearchButton.svelte`, line 48

```svelte
&lt;button on:click={toggleSearch}&gt;
```

This uses the legacy Svelte 4 `on:click` syntax. Every other component in the codebase uses the Svelte 5 `onclick` syntax. This should be `onclick={toggleSearch}`.

### 4b. EditCoursButton.svelte uses deprecated $page store with .subscribe()
**File**: `src\lib\ui\navigators\buttons\EditCoursButton.svelte`, line 29

```svelte
page.subscribe((path) =&gt; {
```

This uses the Svelte 4 `$app/stores` `page` with `.subscribe()`. In Svelte 5, this should use `$app/state`'s `page` (as done in `TalkAdobe.svelte`). The `.subscribe()` call also never calls the unsubscribe function, creating a subscription leak.

### 4c. Sidebar.svelte -- Props without types
**File**: `src\lib\ui\components\Sidebar.svelte`, line 5

```svelte
let { position = "left", menuSelector, sidebarContent } = $props();
```

No interface or type annotation. `menuSelector` and `sidebarContent` are Snippets but not typed as such. Compare with `TutorsShell.svelte` which properly types `children: Snippet`.

### 4d. Menu.svelte -- Props without types
**File**: `src\lib\ui\components\Menu.svelte`, line 3

```svelte
let { menuSelector, menuContent } = $props();
```

Same issue -- no type annotations for the snippet props.

### 4e. CourseVisitCard.svelte -- Missing lang="ts"
**File**: `src\routes\(home)\CourseVisitCard.svelte`, line 1

```svelte
&lt;script&gt;
```

Every other component uses `&lt;script lang="ts"&gt;`. This one uses plain JavaScript, so `courseVisit`, `deleteCourse`, and `starUnstarCourse` props are untyped.

### 4f. LoContext.svelte -- Props inconsistency
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\structure\LoContext.svelte`, line 6

```svelte
let { lo, indent = 0 }: { lo: Lo; indent: number } = $props();
```

Uses inline type annotation instead of the `interface Props` pattern used everywhere else.

---

## 5. PERFORMANCE ISSUES

### 5a. SearchButton.svelte -- MutationObserver on document.body with subtree
**File**: `src\lib\ui\navigators\buttons\SearchButton.svelte`, lines 38-42

```js
const observer = new MutationObserver(checkForNavigation);
observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });
```

This fires the callback on every single DOM mutation in the entire page. This is extremely expensive -- every Svelte component update, every transition frame, every text change triggers this observer. The stated purpose (checking if URL includes "/search/") could be accomplished with `afterNavigate` or by subscribing to the page store.

### 5b. TalkMozilla.svelte -- pdfjs-dist imported eagerly
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\TalkMozilla.svelte`, lines 2-3

```svelte
import * as pdfjs from "pdfjs-dist";
import FileSaver from "file-saver";
```

These are heavy libraries imported at the top level. The `TalkClient.svelte` wrapper does lazy-load this component with `{#await import(...)}`, which partially mitigates the issue. However, `FileSaver` is also eagerly imported when it is only used in the `downloadPdf()` function -- it should be dynamically imported when actually needed.

### 5c. $effect with async work in time/+page.svelte
**File**: `src\routes\(course-reader)\time\[courseid]\+page.svelte`, lines 17-34

```svelte
$effect(() =&gt; {
  const courseId = currentCourse.value?.courseId;
  const studentLogin = tutorsId.value?.login;
  if (!courseId || !studentLogin) return;
  isLoading = true;
  TutorsTime.loadStudentTime(courseId, studentLogin, null, null)
    .then(...)
```

Using `.then()` inside `$effect` means the effect cannot be properly cleaned up. If the reactive dependencies change while the promise is in flight, there is a race condition -- an older response could overwrite a newer one. This should use an AbortController or at minimum a stale-check pattern.

---

## 6. STATE MANAGEMENT ISSUES

### 6a. Video.svelte -- Redundant $effect
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\Video.svelte`, lines 27-31

```svelte
let videoConfig = $state(getVideoConfig(lo));

$effect(() =&gt; {
  videoConfig = getVideoConfig(lo);
});
```

The `$state` initializer already sets `videoConfig`. The `$effect` immediately re-runs `getVideoConfig(lo)`. This should simply be `let videoConfig = $derived(getVideoConfig(lo))`.

### 6b. TalkMozilla.svelte -- $effect triggers side effects on every reactive change
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\TalkMozilla.svelte`, lines 33-38

```svelte
$effect(() =&gt; {
  loading = true;
  url = lo.pdf;
  pageNum = 1;
  loadDoc();
});
```

This effect depends on `lo` (via `lo.pdf`), but it also writes to `loading`, `url`, and `pageNum` -- all `$state` variables. Setting `$state` inside `$effect` that reads other `$state` can create infinite loops in some scenarios. It also reloads the document whenever any property of `lo` changes, not just `lo.pdf`.

### 6c. TalkAdobe.svelte -- $effect with console.log left in
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\TalkAdobe.svelte`, lines 66-71

```svelte
$effect(() =&gt; {
  console.log(page.data?.lo?.pdf);
  if (mounted &amp;&amp; page.data?.lo?.pdf) {
    displayPDF();
  }
});
```

Debug `console.log` left in production code. Also, the effect depends on `page.data?.lo?.pdf` but the initial `onMount` has already called `displayPDF()` -- there could be double-rendering.

### 6d. SearchButton.svelte -- Module-level browser API access
**File**: `src\lib\ui\navigators\buttons\SearchButton.svelte`, line 6

```svelte
let isSearching = sessionStorage.getItem("isSearching") === "true";
```

This runs at module evaluation time (not inside `onMount`), which will throw during SSR since `sessionStorage` does not exist on the server. This component appears to only be rendered client-side due to conditional rendering in `MainNavigator.svelte`, but it is still fragile.

### 6e. Context.svelte -- Mutation of props
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\structure\Context.svelte`, lines 16-21

```svelte
// svelte-ignore non_reactive_update
let loContext = lo;
if (loContext) {
  while (loContext.type !== "topic" &amp;&amp; loContext.type !== "course") {
    loContext = loContext.parentLo!;
  }
}
```

The `svelte-ignore non_reactive_update` comment suppresses a warning that `loContext` will not react to changes in `lo`. If `lo` changes (e.g., navigation), the context panel will show stale data. This should use `$derived`.

### 6f. LoContext.svelte -- Direct mutation of props
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\structure\LoContext.svelte`, lines 9-16

```svelte
if (lo?.toc) {
  lo.toc.forEach((child: Lo) =&gt; {
    if (child.route.endsWith("/")) {
      child.route = child.route.slice(0, -1);
    }
    ...
  });
}
```

This mutates the `lo` prop's children directly (modifying `child.route`). In Svelte 5, props should be treated as read-only. This mutation could cause subtle bugs and unexpected behavior in other components that share the same `Lo` objects.

---

## 7. SECURITY -- MISCELLANEOUS

### 7a. TalkAdobe.svelte -- Script injection from CDN
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\TalkAdobe.svelte`, lines 39-43

```svelte
const script = document.createElement("script");
script.src = "https://acrobatservices.adobe.com/view-sdk/viewer.js";
document.head.appendChild(script);
```

Dynamically injecting a script tag without SRI (Subresource Integrity). If the CDN is compromised, arbitrary JavaScript would execute in the app context. The KaTeX CSS links in `Lab.svelte` and `Note.svelte` do have `integrity` attributes, showing the pattern is known but not consistently applied.

### 7b. TalkMozilla.svelte -- Missing type annotation on event parameter
**File**: `src\lib\ui\learning-objects\content\TalkMozilla.svelte`, line 44

```svelte
function keypressInput(e) {
```

This is the only event handler in the codebase without a TypeScript type annotation (the file does have `lang="ts"`). Minor but inconsistent.

---

## SUMMARY OF SEVERITY

**Critical (fix immediately)**:
- 14 unsanitized `{@html}` usages with no DOMPurify anywhere in the codebase
- SearchButton.svelte MutationObserver on entire DOM tree, never disconnected

**High (should fix soon)**:
- Multiple event listener leaks (Cards.svelte, SearchButton.svelte, TalkAdobe.svelte)
- WebSocket connections in presence service never closed on re-listen
- Connect service interval started but never stopped
- EditCoursButton.svelte store subscription leak

**Medium (plan to fix)**:
- Accessibility: empty alt text on meaningful images, missing aria-labels, non-semantic `&lt;prose&gt;` element, suppressed a11y warnings
- Mixed Svelte 4/5 patterns (`on:click` vs `onclick`, `$app/stores` vs `$app/state`)
- Multiple untyped component props
- $effect misuse (async work without cleanup, redundant effects)

